{
 "note": "Sea Play on the Bay (the Busselton Foreshore Playspace, PLAN E 2018), the foreshore playground west of the jetty, from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), OSM and photos. A big red-brown timber clipper ship half sunk in white sand and heeled towards the beach, three white steel masts with yards and a timber crow's nest, a grey timber wharf off its stern with old wharf piles, a blue whale in the blue wet-play area to the north-west, an orange steel squid (lattice mantle and tentacle arches) to the north-east, sandstone boulders and low concrete seat walls. Approximated in blocks and panels: masts, yards and rigging are stepped bars, arches are three bars; the curved hull, lattice and nets want a Blender layer. Only the stern castle is a block, so the base clears just a small spot and keeps the Norfolk pines. Metres: x along the ship from the stern (bearing 76), y across it towards the beach (bearing 346).",
